---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, MOMENT_UTC, SITE_ORIGIN, TONE_HZ } from '../config';

const instant = new Date(MOMENT_UTC).toISOString().replace('T', ' ').replace('.000Z', ' UTC');
---

<Base
  title="Manourying — Press"
  description="A plain description of the project, the facts worth checking, and how to reach a person."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Press</p>
  <h1 class="serif">For anyone writing about this</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Take anything on this page and use it without asking. If something here is unclear or you
    think it is wrong, say so — a correction before publication is worth more to us than a
    flattering piece.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>One paragraph</h2>
    <blockquote>
      Manourying is an art project built around a single instant. At the September equinox —
      the moment the whole planet shares equal day and night — everybody holding the app makes the
      same sound at the same time: four seconds of an open vowel at about {TONE_HZ} Hz, then their
      own name, then ten seconds of silence. Sixteen seconds in total. The app is invite-only, does
      almost nothing until the day, and sends exactly two notifications in the months beforehand.
      Then it happens, and it is over for six months.
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Facts worth checking</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>The instant</dt><dd class="mono">{instant}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Duration</dt><dd class="mono">16 seconds</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Reference pitch</dt><dd class="mono">{TONE_HZ} Hz</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cadence</dt><dd class="mono">Twice a year, at each equinox</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Entry</dt><dd class="mono">Invite-only · three per seat · non-replenishing</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd class="mono">iOS and Android</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd class="mono">Free · nothing sold · no advertising</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Three things we will not let you print</h2>
    <p>
      Not because they are unflattering, but because they are false, and we would rather you heard
      it from us:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>That it will register on seismometers.</strong> It will not. A billion voices do
        not move a seismometer. Dense urban seismic networks do show human-activity signatures —
        well documented during the 2020 lockdowns — and that is a genuinely interesting story, but
        it is not the same claim.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>That it is perfectly simultaneous.</strong> Sound travels 343 m/s. Two people
        340 metres apart cannot hear each other at the same instant; physics forbids it. The
        project treats that as the interesting part rather than pretending otherwise.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>That it is a protest, a religion, or a brand campaign.</strong> Nobody is asked to
        believe anything, oppose anything, join anything, or buy anything.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> — a real person, usually within a day.
      For fact-checking on a deadline, say so in the subject line.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      Canonical explainer: <a href={`${SITE_ORIGIN}/what-this-is`}>{SITE_ORIGIN}/what-this-is</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-block: 14px 20px;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: clamp(26px, 4vw, 38px);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--bone);
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--mist);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    line-height: 1.72;
  }
  p + p {
    margin-top: 0.9em;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--brass);
    color: var(--bone);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0.6em;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.7em;
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--bone);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .facts {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
  }
  .facts > div {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
    padding-block: 10px;
  }
  .facts dt {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
    min-width: 11rem;
  }
  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bone);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .fine {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
</style>
